# The Changing AI Landscape

AI has been around for decades, but what has changed is how visible, interactive, and accessible it has become.

👉 Click each time period to explore how AI has evolved and how those changes have shown up in schools.

<strong>Note:</strong> This timeline primarily reflects the evolution of AI tools and their impact within U.S. schools and classrooms. The pace of adoption, access to technology, and educational experiences with AI may differ across countries and regions.

## AI Timeline

<div style="position:relative; padding-left:38px;">

<!-- timeline line -->
<div style="position:absolute; left:14px; top:8px; bottom:8px; width:3px; background:#D9DDE3; border-radius:2px;"></div>

<!-- 2010–2018 -->
<div style="position:relative; margin-bottom:18px;">

<div style="position:absolute; left:-32px; top:20px; width:14px; height:14px; background:#7a6fa6; border-radius:50%; border:3px solid white; box-shadow:0 0 0 2px #D9DDE3;"></div>

<details style="border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; background:white;">

<summary style="cursor:pointer; padding:16px 18px; background-color:#F7F8FA; font-size:18px; font-weight:600;">
~2010–2018: Background and Assistive AI
</summary>

<div style="padding:18px 24px; background:white; border-top:1px solid #E5E7EB;">

<div style="display:flex; gap:18px; align-items:stretch;">

<div style="flex:1; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; background:#f3f1fa; border:1px solid #ddd6f3; border-radius:10px; padding:14px 16px;">
<p style="margin-top:0;"><strong>Technology shift</strong></p>
<p style="margin-bottom:0;">
AI-powered features appeared in tools like Google Search, Netflix recommendations, Siri, spellcheck, voice typing, translation, and adaptive learning software.
</p>
</div>

<div style="flex:1; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; background:#eef7f9; border:1px solid #cfe7ec; border-radius:10px; padding:14px 16px;">
<p style="margin-top:0;"><strong>Classroom shift</strong></p>
<p style="margin-bottom:0;">
Teachers saw AI supporting accessibility and personalization through tools like autocorrect, speech-to-text, translation, and adaptive practice platforms, but most of these systems operated quietly in the background and were rarely discussed explicitly as “AI.”
</p>
</div>

</div>
</div>
</details>
</div>

<!-- 2019–2021 -->
<div style="position:relative; margin-bottom:18px;">

<div style="position:absolute; left:-32px; top:20px; width:14px; height:14px; background:#5aaebc; border-radius:50%; border:3px solid white; box-shadow:0 0 0 2px #D9DDE3;"></div>

<details style="border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; background:white;">

<summary style="cursor:pointer; padding:16px 18px; background-color:#F7F8FA; font-size:18px; font-weight:600;">
~2019–2021: AI-Assisted Writing and Content Support
</summary>

<div style="padding:18px 24px; background:white; border-top:1px solid #E5E7EB;">

<div style="display:flex; gap:18px; align-items:stretch;">

<div style="flex:1; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; background:#f3f1fa; border:1px solid #ddd6f3; border-radius:10px; padding:14px 16px;">
<p style="margin-top:0;"><strong>Technology shift</strong></p>
<p style="margin-bottom:0;">
AI systems became much better at predicting, revising, and generating text, powering tools that could autocomplete sentences, suggest rewrites, summarize information, and support more natural interactions with language.
</p>
</div>

<div style="flex:1; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; background:#eef7f9; border:1px solid #cfe7ec; border-radius:10px; padding:14px 16px;">
<p style="margin-top:0;"><strong>Classroom shift</strong></p>
<p style="margin-bottom:0;">
Teachers began seeing AI-supported writing tools become more common in products like Grammarly, Google Docs Smart Compose, and adaptive learning platforms. Students could now use AI not just for spelling or grammar, but to support brainstorming, revision, and drafting—raising new questions about authorship, originality, and academic integrity.
</p>
</div>

</div>
</div>
</details>
</div>

<!-- 2022–Present -->
<div style="position:relative; margin-bottom:12px;">

<div style="position:absolute; left:-32px; top:20px; width:14px; height:14px; background:#7a6fa6; border-radius:50%; border:3px solid white; box-shadow:0 0 0 2px #D9DDE3;"></div>

<details style="border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; background:white;">

<summary style="cursor:pointer; padding:16px 18px; background-color:#F7F8FA; font-size:18px; font-weight:600;">
~2022–Present: Conversational AI in Everyday Classrooms
</summary>

<div style="padding:18px 24px; background:white; border-top:1px solid #E5E7EB;">

<div style="display:flex; gap:18px; align-items:stretch;">

<div style="flex:1; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; background:#f3f1fa; border:1px solid #ddd6f3; border-radius:10px; padding:14px 16px;">
<p style="margin-top:0;"><strong>Technology shift</strong></p>
<p style="margin-bottom:0;">
Public tools like ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, and Copilot made AI much more visible, interactive, and easy to access.
</p>
</div>

<div style="flex:1; font-size:15px; line-height:1.5; color:#555; background:#eef7f9; border:1px solid #cfe7ec; border-radius:10px; padding:14px 16px;">
<p style="margin-top:0;"><strong>Classroom shift</strong></p>
<p style="margin-bottom:0;">
Students and teachers increasingly began using AI directly for explanations, drafting, feedback, lesson planning, and practice. AI shifted from a mostly invisible support tool to something students actively interact with every day, changing conversations about teaching, learning, assessment, and responsible use.
</p>
</div>

</div>
</div>
</details>
</div>

</div>

<br>

> **💬 Quick Reflection:** When did you first notice AI in your school/classroom? In your everyday life?
MARKDOWN
